  "summary": "DIR-099 Phase Two plan (Master UI/UX Transformation - screenshot-first audit + remediation + objective scoring). S1: build scripts/ux-audit.mjs - a Playwright audit engine that, for every review unit at all 7 viewports, measures real defects: horizontal overflow, console errors, failed network requests, and accessibility basics (landmark regions, exactly-one-h1, image alt text, form control labels, focus-visible affordance, touch-target >= 44x44px). S2: run the audit across all 58 units and record findings + an objective score per unit using the mandated 6-dimension rubric (Visual consistency 25 / Responsive 20 / Usability+navigation 20 / Functional correctness 20 / Accessibility+feedback 10 / Performance 5); write results into inventory.json (defects[], score, status). S3: remediate the highest-severity real defects at root cause (fix the source component, never a CSS override that hides the symptom), highest user impact first. S4: re-run the audit and npm run test:ux-gates and npm test; mark a unit ACCEPTED only when its evidence-backed score is >= 98/100 and it has no unresolved P0/P1 defect. S5: submit evidence; units not yet at >=98 remain INVENTORIED/IN_REVIEW and the director issues the next batch. Acceptance: audit engine runs, scores recorded for every unit, at least the top-priority units remediated and ACCEPTED at >=98, npm test + ux-gates green, src/cv-templates 0-byte diff."
}